Learned counsel submits that no case for grant of employment is made out by the petitioner on account of three counts:
(a) Much time has elapsed from the date of acquisition;
(b) Petitioner was minor on the date of acquisition, and (c) There is no legal obligation on the part of the respondents to give any employment to the petitioner as the land was acquired by State under Land Acquisition Act and the case of the petitioner does not fall under policy of the respondent - BCCL in its Re-settlement and Rehabilitation policy.

7. This court is of the considered view that no case for grant of employment is made out by the petitioner on account of three counts:
(i) Much time has elapsed from the date of acquisition and the petitioner has approached this court after much delay;
(ii) Petitioner was minor on the date of acquisition, and (iii) There is no legal obligation on the part of the respondents to give any employment to the petitioner as the land was acquired by State under Land Acquisition Act and the case of the petitioner does not fall under policy of the respondent - BCCL in its Re-settlement and Rehabilitation policy.
